    <name>
      <text>Partial derivatives: Example 5</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \(p(y_{1}, y_{2}, y_{3})={@pp@}\)</p>
<p>and calculate \(\frac{\partial p}{\partial y_{3}}\) at the point \((y_{1}, y_{2}, y_{3})=({@xx@}, {@yy@},{@zz@})\).</p>
<p> <b>Step 1:</b> calculate \(\frac{\partial p}{\partial y_{3}}\) using the quotient rule. </p>
\(\frac{\partial p}{\partial y_{3}}=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p> <b>Step 2:</b> Plugging in the point \((y_{1}, y_{2}, y_{3})=({@xx@}, {@yy@},{@zz@})\). </p>
\(\frac{\partial p}{\partial y_{3}} ({@xx@}, {@yy@},{@zz@})=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked solution</b></p>
Let \(p(y_{1}, y_{2}, y_{3})={@pp@}\)
 <p> <b>Step 1: </b>calculate \(\frac{\partial p}{\partial y_{3}}\) using the quotient rule.</p> 
<p>
\(
\begin{align}
\frac{\partial p}{\partial y_{3}} & = \frac{\partial }{\partial y_{3}} \left( {@pp@}\right) \\

& = \frac{\frac{\partial }{\partial y_{3}} ({@aa*y1^nn*y2^mm*y3^ee@}) \cdot ({@bb*y1+cc*y2+dd*y3@})-\frac{\partial }{\partial y_{3}} ({@bb*y1+cc*y2+dd*y3@}) \cdot ({@aa*y1^nn*y2^mm*y3^ee @})}{@(bb*y1+cc*y2+dd*y3)^2@}\\

& = {@ta_1@}
\end{align}
\)</p>

 <p> <b>Step 2: </b> Plugging in the point \((y_{1}, y_{2}, y_{3})=({@xx@}, {@yy@},{@zz@})\). </p> 
\(\frac{\partial p}{\partial y_{3}} ({@xx@}, {@yy@},{@zz@})={@ta_2@}\)]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
